ngredients to our wet but make sure  that you add them one cup at a time this  is going to ensure that all of the flour  gets incorporated evenly and that you  don't overwork the batter the reason why  you don't want to overwork your batter  is because that's going to produce a  really dense cake and that is not going  to get you invited back to the potluck  all right so i've gotten to the bottom  of my bowl let's add that to our batter  [Music]  all right  the batter looks and smells fantastic  but there's one more important step that  we have to do before we put it in the  oven  i'm using a butt pan to make my pound  cake my grandma use a bun pan i'm using  a bun pan you can use whatever you want  as long as it holds 14 and a half cups  now the thing to remember is you want to  make sure that your pan is prepared so  that the cake doesn't stick i'm spraying  my pan with cooking spray and i'm being  generous with it you want to make sure  you get that spray in every crevice of  the pan i'm going to lightly sprinkle my  pan with flour and i like to rotate to  make sure that the entire pan is evenly  coated next i pat as i rotate to make  sure that the flour distributes across  the pan  all right this looks evenly coated now  i'm going to add in my batter this looks  really silky and smooth and we're not  adding my batter i just like to add it  around the bunk pan in a circle  to make sure that we get it evenly  distributed  a lot of air made it into my batter when  i pour it into my pan so a good trick to  get rid of that excess air is to give it  a shake and to drop it  you only need to do that a couple of  times and then it's ready to bake i have  my oven set to 300 degrees i'm gonna  throw this in there for an hour and a  half  [Music]  while my pound cake is in the oven i'm  going to show you how to make a citrus  glaze now i'm going with citrus because  it's in season during the winter in a  large bowl i'm going to combine my  powdered sugar my milk  melted butter  vanilla extract  the zest of a lemon some lime zest and  finally i'm going to zest my orange and  yes this is an orange even though it  looks yellow let's mix it all up until  it's well combined  this glaze looks perfect all i have to  do now is wait for my cake to be done  our cake has been out of the oven for 10  minutes cooling off now it's time to  flip and release it  okay guys now's the time of truth  oh  it's beautiful completely clean okay you  guys see that  it looks incredible  now we're gonna let it cool for another  30 minutes before we add our glaze  oh  this is my favorite part adding that  glaze  i cannot wait to try a bite  ah  look at that oh my goodness  this cake is so  delicious the outside kind of forms this  crust that's nice and sugary and then  the inside of the cake is moist and  buttery and decadent and then that  citrus glaze just up  it is so good and when you guys try this  cake it is about to blow your mind  all right guys so today i showed you how  to make the ultimate pound cake with a  citrus glaze i'm really interested to  hear what you think about this pound  cake leave a comment down below or hit  me up on instagram at mikko in the dish  until next time peace  oh yes  do  you
 

